WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.200
First day, and they've asked me to check on a station.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.780
Where do I even start?

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.870
Start with the search up top.

4
00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:12.110
Type a name, a station number or an ALERT address, and pick

5
00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.540
it from the list.

6
00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:17.070
That opens its card on the map.

7
00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:20.790
First, whose station it is; then its health:

8
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.730
when it was last heard, and anything wrong.

9
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.240
And how do I see what it's been reading?

10
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:32.050
Under Data: its readings, every gauge on the same river, and the

11
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.470
rain gauges round it, each a plot a press away.

12
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.360
Under All actions, the way in:

13
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.360
directions to it, and Street View and Google Earth to see it

14
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.310
before you go.

15
00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.660
What if I'm already out there?

16
00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:51.590
Then Nearby lists the stations closest to where you're standing.

17
00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:54.060
Press one, and it's the same card.

18
00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:58.190
That's the job. Now have a go yourself:

19
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.230
press Show me on the app, and I'll walk you through it.
